Common Garage Door Problems in Ocala
Garage doors operate through a combination of springs, cables, rollers, tracks, hinges, sensors, and opener components. Regular use can eventually cause these parts to wear or fail.
Some common problems homeowners may experience include:
    • Broken or weakened garage door springs
    • Frayed or damaged cables
    • Bent or misaligned tracks
    • Worn rollers and hinges
    • Garage door opener failures
    • Faulty safety sensors
    • Damaged garage door panels
    • Doors that become stuck or uneven
Addressing these problems early may help prevent additional stress on other components.
