Signs Your Garage Door Needs Repair
Many garage doors show warning signs before completely failing.
Grinding, squeaking, scraping, or banging sounds may indicate worn or loose components. A door that shakes, moves unevenly, or operates more slowly than usual should also be inspected.
Other warning signs include a garage door that reverses unexpectedly, does not close completely, feels unusually heavy, or fails to respond consistently to the opener.
Visible cable damage or a broken spring requires particular attention. Because springs and cables operate under substantial tension, homeowners should avoid attempting potentially dangerous repairs themselves.
